    "updated_at": "2023-03-06T22:22:52Z",
    "body": "> I wrote this because this is how it is implemented in chromium:\r\n> \r\n> * https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/html_collection.cc;l=263-268;drc=e20bf9387f49c3a0b208bad26dc8efc0dc214e96\r\n> * https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/document.cc;l=7248-7250;drc=83dedea96a08faa03c3e28820efeee3a2781d197\r\n> \r\n> I suppose that using an HTMLCollection is not necessary, and that the spec could just say to traverse over every element in the document or something. Or better yet, get rid of \"popover invokers\" entirely and just inline the one usage of that term with something that looks at every element in the document.\r\n\r\nI don't have a problem with using an HTMLCollection, but the first link seems to filter down to stuff that has the popovertarget attribute, and I don't see that anywhere in the spec algorithm. Right now, as I read it, every button in the document is a popover invoker, which seems wrong?",
